    <!-- Verification Guide -->
    <section class="section verification-guide">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Before You Apply: Your Verification Kit</h2>
        <ul class="guide-list">
          <li><strong>Use your college email if you have one.</strong> Microsoft 365, Notion, Altium and MATLAB check your email domain first, and it is the quickest route everywhere else.</li>
          <li><strong>No college email? Prepare dated proof.</strong> GitHub accepts a student ID, transcript, enrollment letter or class schedule that shows your name, your college and a current date.</li>
          <li><strong>Know what usually fails.</strong> Undated ID cards, screenshots of emails, and admission letters for a future term do not prove current enrollment.</li>
          <li><strong>Match the details.</strong> Type your name and college exactly as they appear on the document, and submit one sharp photo.</li>
          <li><strong>For GitHub, allow location and turn off your VPN.</strong> Applying from campus or on mobile data helps.</li>
          <li><strong>Do not retry blindly.</strong> Fix the document first, then contact the provider's support instead of resubmitting the same file.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

